DECISIONS 339, CODEGEN.md §2.1: an empty `open` is refused (`openEmpty`): omit it to keep every enum closed; a value that is no list is `kind`.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A destination.
enum Dst { str, sta }

emit go { out: "@sovcommon/a", mode: types, open: [] }
-- b/b.canon --
package b

/// A destination.
enum Dst { str, sta }

emit go { out: "@sovcommon/b", mode: types, open: Dst }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8009]  a/a.canon:6:51
  open of emit go is an empty list: omit open to keep every enum closed

error[E8009]  b/b.canon:6:51
  option open of emit go must be a list of enum names

2 errors, 0 warnings in 2 packages (…)
